{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given the `root` of a binary search tree and a node `p` in it, return the **in-order successor** of p — the node with the smallest value **greater than** p.val — or null if p holds the largest value."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/1b1f264c-bd3d-4df0-8cb8-0b827b9c3f7f.svg",
      "alt": "The tree 20, 8, 22, 4, 12, null, null, null, null, 10, 14 with p = 14. Walking down from the root for values above 14: 20 is bigger, so it's a candidate, go left; 8 is smaller, go right; 12 is smaller, go right; 14 is not bigger, go right and stop. The last candidate, 20, is the successor.",
      "width": 755,
      "height": 503,
      "scene": {
