    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [2, 1, 3], p = 1                                   ->  2\nroot = [5, 3, 6, 2, 4, null, null, 1], p = 6              ->  null   (6 is the largest)\nroot = [20, 8, 22, 4, 12, null, null, null, null, 10, 14], p = 8   ->  10\nroot = [20, 8, 22, 4, 12, null, null, null, null, 10, 14], p = 14  ->  20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. In-order walk, return the node after p"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function inorderSuccessor(root, p) {\n  let prev = null, answer = null;\n  const inorder = (node) => {\n    if (node === null || answer !== null) return;\n    inorder(node.left);\n    if (answer === null && prev === p) answer = node;   // the node right after p\n    prev = node;\n    inorder(node.right);\n  };\n  inorder(root);\n  return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def inorder_successor(root, p):\n    prev = answer = None\n\n    def inorder(node):\n        nonlocal prev, answer\n        if node is None or answer is not None:\n            return\n        inorder(node.left)\n        if answer is None and prev is p:\n            answer = node                 # the node right after p\n        prev = node\n        inorder(node.right)\n\n    inorder(root)\n    return answer"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode prev, answer;\n\nTreeNode inorderSuccessor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p) {\n    prev = answer = null;\n    inorder(root, p);\n    return answer;\n}\n\nvoid inorder(TreeNode node, TreeNode p) {\n    if (node == null || answer != null) return;\n    inorder(node.left, p);\n    if (answer == null && prev == p) answer = node;   // the node right after p\n    prev = node;\n    inorder(node.right, p);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void inorder(TreeNode* node, TreeNode* p, TreeNode*& prev, TreeNode*& answer) {\n    if (node == nullptr || answer != nullptr) return;\n    inorder(node->left, p, prev, answer);\n    if (answer == nullptr && prev == p) answer = node;   // the node right after p\n    prev = node;\n    inorder(node->right, p, prev, answer);\n}\n\nTreeNode* inorderSuccessor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p) {\n    TreeNode *prev = nullptr, *answer = nullptr;\n    inorder(root, p, prev, answer);\n    return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(h).** Works on any binary tree — the ordering is never used."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Use p's right subtree, or the last left turn"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "If p has a **right subtree**, the successor is that subtree's leftmost node. If not, it's the nearest ancestor for which p lies in the **left** subtree — the last node where a search for p turned left."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function inorderSuccessor(root, p) {\n  if (p.right !== null) {                  // leftmost node of the right subtree\n    let node = p.right;\n    while (node.left !== null) node = node.left;\n    return node;\n  }\n  let answer = null, node = root;          // search for p; remember the last left turn\n  while (node !== p) {\n    if (p.val < node.val) {\n      answer = node;\n      node = node.left;\n    } else node = node.right;\n  }\n  return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def inorder_successor(root, p):\n    if p.right is not None:               # leftmost node of the right subtree\n        node = p.right\n        while node.left is not None:\n            node = node.left\n        return node\n    answer, node = None, root             # search for p; remember the last left turn\n    while node is not p:\n        if p.val < node.val:\n            answer = node\n            node = node.left\n        else:\n            node = node.right\n    return answer"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode inorderSuccessor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p) {\n    if (p.right != null) {                           // leftmost node of the right subtree\n        TreeNode node = p.right;\n        while (node.left != null) node = node.left;\n        return node;\n    }\n    TreeNode answer = null, node = root;             // search for p; remember the last left turn\n    while (node != p) {\n        if (p.val < node.val) {\n            answer = node;\n            node = node.left;\n        } else node = node.right;\n    }\n    return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "TreeNode* inorderSuccessor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p) {\n    if (p->right != nullptr) {                       // leftmost node of the right subtree\n        TreeNode* node = p->right;\n        while (node->left != nullptr) node = node->left;\n        return node;\n    }\n    TreeNode *answer = nullptr, *node = root;        // search for p; remember the last left turn\n    while (node != p) {\n        if (p->val < node->val) {\n            answer = node;\n            node = node->left;\n        } else node = node->right;\n    }\n    return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h), space O(1).** Two cases, each one walk down."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "3. One walk: the smallest value above p.val"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Both cases collapse into one loop: walk from the root, and every node **bigger than p.val** is a candidate — keep it and go left for a smaller one. A node not bigger than p.val can't be the answer — go right. It's the **ceil** search from the Floor and Ceil lesson, with strictly greater."
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "inorder-successor-bst",
      "caption": "Bigger than p: a candidate, go left. Not bigger: go right."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function inorderSuccessor(root, p) {\n  let answer = null;\n  let node = root;\n  while (node !== null) {\n    if (node.val > p.val) {\n      answer = node;                       // bigger than p: a candidate, look for a smaller one\n      node = node.left;\n    } else {\n      node = node.right;                   // not bigger: the successor is to the right\n    }\n  }\n  return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def inorder_successor(root, p):\n    answer = None\n    node = root\n    while node is not None:\n        if node.val > p.val:\n            answer = node                 # bigger than p: a candidate, look for a smaller one\n            node = node.left\n        else:\n            node = node.right             # not bigger: the successor is to the right\n    return answer"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode inorderSuccessor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p) {\n    TreeNode answer = null;\n    TreeNode node = root;\n    while (node != null) {\n        if (node.val > p.val) {\n            answer = node;                           // bigger than p: a candidate, look for a smaller one\n            node = node.left;\n        } else {\n            node = node.right;                       // not bigger: the successor is to the right\n        }\n    }\n    return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "TreeNode* inorderSuccessor(TreeNode* root, TreeNode* p) {\n    TreeNode* answer = nullptr;\n    TreeNode* node = root;\n    while (node != nullptr) {\n        if (node->val > p->val) {\n            answer = node;                           // bigger than p: a candidate, look for a smaller one\n            node = node->left;\n        } else {\n            node = node->right;                      // not bigger: the successor is to the right\n        }\n    }\n    return answer;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(h), space O(1).** It never even needs p's node — only its value."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "In-order walk, return the node after p",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "It may visit **every node**: the ordering is never used.",
          "space": "O(h)",
          "spaceWhy": "The recursion or stack follows **one path**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Use p's right subtree, or the last left turn",
          "time": "O(h)",
          "timeWhy": "Either case is **one walk down** the tree.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "A loop with **one remembered node**."
        },
        {
          "approach": "One walk: the smallest value above p.val",
          "time": "O(h)",
          "timeWhy": "Each step goes **left or right once**, like a search.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "Only the **best candidate so far**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**p is the largest value** — null.",
        "**p has a right subtree** — the leftmost node there.",
        "**p is a leaf in a left subtree** — the answer is an ancestor, possibly the root.",
        "**A single node** — null."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Inorder Predecessor** — mirror it: nodes smaller than p are candidates, go right.",
        "**Inorder Successor II** — nodes have parent pointers and no root: go to the right subtree's leftmost, or climb until you come up from a left child.",
        "**Delete Node in a BST** — the two-children case replaces a node with its successor (Pattern 1)."
      ]
    }
